        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "update consistently improves over the initialization at 1%, 5%, 10%, and 20% sampling. The gap is visible at low sampling rates and grows slightly with more observations, whereas the initialization curve tends to plateau at higher rates. These results indicate that the update stage, informed by the concurrent map reconstruction, adds clear value beyond the PG-KMeans initializer and yields lower mean localization error across sampling levels.",
