                    93.0,
                    952.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "We evaluate RadioTrace at extremely low sampling rates 0.1% and 0.05%. On a 256×256 grid (65,536 pixels), this corresponds to roughly 66 and 33 measurements, respectively. As shown in Table VII, at sampling rate of 0.1%, we obtain NMSE 0.0435, RMSE 0.0435, SSIM 0.9307, and PSNR 29.84 dB; the mean Tx error improves from 24.78 m at initialization to 20.45 m after refinement ( $ \\approx $ 4.33 m reduction). At 0.05%, performance drops as expected (NMSE 0.0675, RMSE 0.0592, SSIM 0.9087, PSNR 27.40 dB), while localization still improves from 41.28 m to 33.88 m ( $ \\approx $ 7.40 m reduction). These results show that RadioTrace remains effective even when only very limited measurements are available.",
            "block_bbox": [
                90,
                959,
                604,
                1271
            ],
            "block_id": 7,
            "block_order": 3,
            "group_id": 7,
