                ],
                [
                    1131.0,
                    1042.0
                ],
                [
                    1131.0,
                    1281.0
                ],
                [
                    617.0,
                    1281.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "As the number of Tx R increases, the only additional computations introduced are the generation of the R soft Gaussian Tx maps and the calculation of their gradients with respect to the Tx coordinates. Since these are simple, low-dimensional mathematical operations, their overhead is strictly negligible compared to the heavy neural network evaluations of the diffusion backbone. Therefore, an increase in R adds practically zero computational burden to the overall inference pipeline.",
